    <string name="login_dialog_local_information">Information is only saved locally and used for HN API.</string>
    <string name="login_dialog_how_it_works">How does login work?</string>
    <string name="login_dialog_information">Since Hacker News does not supply an official API for actions which require login, Harmonic cannot authenticate once and obtain a secret token to use in the future. Instead, actions which require login are performed by sending HTTPS POST requests to Hacker News with your username and password in the request body. This means your password must be stored on your device. It is stored encrypted using AES-256 GCM with management carried out by Google’s AndroidX Security library, and is only used in HTTPS POST form bodies sent to news.ycombinator.com.</string>
    <string name="login_dialog_troubleshooting">If you have issues with login, try the official HN website to confirm whether the issue is with Harmonic or the website.</string>
